<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/rajah-salalila"><span class="enc-name">Rajah Salalila</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rajah Salalila is remembered in tradition as the first ruler of the Bruneian-allied dynasty of Maynila, set up around 1500 after Sultan Bolkiah of Brunei is said to…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/rajah-siagu"><span class="enc-name">Rajah Siagu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rajah Siagu was the ruler of Butuan in northern Mindanao who, with Rajah Kolambu of Limasawa, met Ferdinand Magellan's expedition in March 1521.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rajah-sulayman"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rajah-sulayman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rajah Sulayman</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rajah Sulayman was a ruler of Maynila who shared power with his uncle Rajah Matanda in the 16th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rajahmundry"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rajahmundry.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rajahmundry</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Rajahmundry, officially Rajamahendravaram, is a city on the Godavari River in Andhra Pradesh, India.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/rajakumar"><span class="enc-name">Rajakumar</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rajakumar, also known as Yazakumar, was a prince of Pagan and son of King Kyansittha.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/rajapur"><span class="enc-name">Rajapur</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Rajapur is a port town on the Konkan coast of Maharashtra, western India.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rajaraja-chola-iii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rajaraja-chola-iii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rajaraja Chola III</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rajaraja Chola III was king of the declining Chola dynasty from 1216 to 1256.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rajaraja-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rajaraja-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rajaraja I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rajaraja I was emperor of the Chola Empire of southern India, reigning from 985 to 1014.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rajaraja-narendra"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rajaraja-narendra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rajaraja Narendra</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rajaraja Narendra was a king of the Eastern Chalukyas of Vengi in Andhra, closely allied by marriage with the Chola dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rajaram-i"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/rajaram-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Rajaram I</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rajaram I was the younger son of Shivaji and Chhatrapati of the Maratha kingdom from 1689 to 1700.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/rajashekhara"><span class="enc-name">Rajashekhara</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Rajashekhara was a Sanskrit and Prakrit poet, dramatist and critic at the court of the Gurjara-Pratihara kings Mahendrapala I and Mahipala I at Kannauj.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/rajasinha-i-of-sitawaka"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encycl