rson</span><span class="enc-snip">Ramai Deva was, according to tradition, the Chauhan Rajput founder of the ruling dynasty of Patna in western Odisha in the mid-14th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ramakien"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/ramakien.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ramakien</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ramakien is the Thai national version of the Indian epic Ramayana.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/raman-skirmunt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/raman-skirmunt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Raman Skirmunt</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Raman Skirmunt was a Belarusian landowner and politician, a member of the first Russian State Duma.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ramanatha-hoysala"><span class="enc-name">Ramanatha (Hoysala)</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ramanatha was a Hoysala king who ruled the Tamil territories of the kingdom from Kannanur Kuppam, near Srirangam, after his father Vira Someshvara divided his lands.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ramanathaswamy-temple"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/ramanathaswamy-temple.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ramanathaswamy Temple</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ramanathaswamy Temple is a Hindu temple to Shiva on Rameswaram island in Tamil Nadu, India, one of the twelve jyotirlingas and a major pilgrimage site linked with…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ramanetaka"><span class="enc-name">Ramanetaka</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ramanetaka was a Merina prince and military